hadiths[85]{hadithnumber,text}:
"567","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, There is no Zakat on less than five camels and also there is no Zakat on less than five Awaq (of silver). (5 Awaq = 22 Fransa Riyals of Yemen or 200 Dirhams.) And there is no Zakat on less than five Awsuq. (A special measure of food-grains"
"568","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, There is no Zakat either on a horse or a slave belonging to a Muslim."""""
"569","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) (p.b.u.h) ordered (a person) to collect Zakat, and that person returned and told him that Ibn Jamil, Khalid bin Al-Walid, and `Abbas bin `Abdul Muttalib had refused to give Zakat."" The Prophet said, ""What made Ibn Jamil refuse to give Zakat though he was a poor man, and was made wealthy by Allah and His Apostle ? But you are unfair in asking Zakat from Khalid as he is keeping his armor for Allah's Cause (for Jihad). As for `Abbas bin `Abdul Muttalib, he is the uncle of Allah's Apostle (p.b.u.h) and Zakat is compulsory on him and he should pay it double."""
"570","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said. While I was sleeping"
"571","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Faith (Belief) consists of more than sixty branches (i.e. parts). And Haya (This term ""Haya"" covers a large number of concepts which are to be taken together; amongst them are self respect, modesty, bashfulness, and scruple, etc.) is a part of faith."""
"572","We used tof give one .Sri'of meal one Sd'of barley one,Sri'of dates, one Sd' of lqt(dried yoghurt ttl 9t.) From this (artillery, missiles, page 76), narration religious schof tanks, planes etc.) for-I l2.TheBookof Zakat cottage cheese) one Sd'ofraisins (dried grapes) as Zakdt-ul-Fitr"
"573","In the lifetime of the Prophet d- .=b eJ u-r- we used tof give one Sri'of food one Sri' of dates one Sri' of barley one SA' of raisins (dried grapes) as Sadaqdt-ul-Fitr. And when Mu'6wiya became the Caliph and the wheat was (available in abundance) h said, I think (observe) that one Mudd (of wheat) equals twof Mudds (fand of the above mentioned things)."" Sin of the one whof does not pay ZakAt"""
"574","A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"
"575","he was saying, They are the losers"
"576","r.r Once I went tof the Prophett ps *,tt J- and he said, By Anah in Whose Hands my life is"""
"577","While I was walking with the Prophet (ﷺ) at the Hurra of Medina in the evening, the mountain of Uhud appeared before us. The Prophet (ﷺ) said, O Abu Dhar! I would not like to have gold equal to Uhud (mountain) for me"
"578","Once I went out at night and found Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) walking all alone accompanied by nobody, and I thought that perhaps he disliked that someone should accompany him. So I walked in the shade, away from the moonlight, but the Prophet (ﷺ) looked behind and saw me and said, Who is that?"" I replied"
"579","While I was sitting with some ,r.rnroolof Zo*a"
"580","A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"
"581","The Prophett l-:,4, dr.rJ- came tof know that one of his companions had given the promise of freeing his slave afthis death, but as he had nof property othe thand that slave, the Prophett d- rr arr"
"582","Abu Talha had the largest number of datepalms from amongst the Ansars of Medina. The dearest of his property to him was Bairuha garden which was facing the (Prophet's) Mosque. Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) used to enter it and drink of its good fresh water. When the Holy Verse:-- 'By no means shall you attain righteousness unless you spend (in charity) of that which you love.' (3.92) was revealed, Abu Talha got up and said, O Allah's Messenger (ﷺ)! Allah says: By no means shall you attain righteousness unless you spend of that which you love"
"583","Jabir reported that there happened to pass before Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) an ass the face of which had been cauterised, whereupon he said:Allah has cursed one who has cauterised it (on the face)"
"584","Zainab, the wife of `Abdullah said, I was in the Mosque and saw the Prophet (p.b.u.h) saying"
"585","ru I said, O Allah's Messenger! Shall I ge a reward (in the Hereafter) if I spend of the children of Ab Salama and dof nof leave them like this and like this (i.e. poor) but treat them like my ow children?"" The Prophett /-r"
"586","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, When a Muslim spends something on his family intending to receive Allah's reward it is regarded as Sadaqa for him."""""
"587","Umm 'Atiyya reported:We washed her an odd number of times, i. e. three, five or seven times; and Umm 'Atiyya (further) said: We braided her hair in three plaits"
"588","A mand said tof the Prophett pt 4,.r, u-r- My mothdied suddenly and I thought that if she had lived she would have given alms. So"
"589","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""On every Muslim there is enjoined (a compulsory) Sadaqa (alms)."" They (the people) said, ""If one has nothing?' He said, ""He should work with his hands so that he may benefit himself and give in charity."" They said, ""If he cannot work or does not work?"" He said, ""Then he should help the oppressed unhappy person (by word or action or both)."" They said, ""If he does not do it?"" He said, ""Then he should enjoin what is good (or said what is reasonable).' They said, ""If he does not do that''' He said, ""Then he should refrain from doing evil, for that will be considered for Him as a Sadaqa (charity) . """
"590","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, ""If Allah makes us victorious, our encamping place will be Al-Khaif, the place where the infidels took an oath to be loyal to Heathenism (by boycotting Banu Hashim, the Prophet's folk)."
"591","that the Prophet (ﷺ) gave him some sheep to distribute among his companions to slaughter as sacrifices (`Id--al--Adha). A kid goat was left and he told the Prophet (ﷺ) of that whereupon he said to him, Slaughter it as a sacrifice (on your behalf)."""
"592","I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying, Allah said"
"593","Abu Huraira said, The Prophet (ﷺ) said"
"594","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, The Hour will not be established till two (huge) groups fight against each other"
"595","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, If somebody gives in charity something equal to a date from his honestly earned money ----for nothing ascends to Allah except good---- then Allah will take it in His Right (Hand) and bring it up for its owner as anyone of you brings up a baby horse"
"596","""Save yourself from Hell-fire even by giving half a date-fruit in charity."""
"597","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""There will be none among you but will be talked to by Allah on the Day of Resurrection, without there being an interpreter between him and Him (Allah) . He will look and see nothing ahead of him, and then he will look (again for the second time) in front of him, and the (Hell) Fire will confront him. So, whoever among you can save himself from the Fire, should do so even with one half of a date (to give in charity)."
"598","When we were ordered to give alms, we began to work as porters (to earn something we could give in charity). Abu `Aqil came with one half of a Sa` (special measure for food grains) and another person brought more than he did. So the hypocrites said, Allah is not in need of the alms of this (i.e. Abu `Aqil); and this other person did not give alms but for showing off."" Then Allah revealed:-- 'Those who criticize such of the Believers who give charity voluntarily and those who could not find to give in charity except what is available to them.' (9.79)"""
"599","Abu Huraira said, ""Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, 'No one should prevent his neighbor from fixing a wooden peg in his wall."" Abu Huraira said (to his companions), ""Why do I find you averse to it? By Allah, I certainly will narrate it to you."""
"600","Ibn Samura al-'Adawi reported:I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) say, and he then narrated (the above-mentioned hadith)"
"601","A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"
"602","This hadith has been transmitted by Ibrahim b. Sa'd b. Malik on the authority of his father"
"603","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, If a woman gives in charity from her house meals without wasting (i.e. being extravagant)"
"604","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""A woman should not fast (optional fasts) except with her husband's permission if he is at home (staying with her)."
"605","Anas reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If the son of Adam were to possess two valleys of riches. he would long for the third one. And the stomach of the son of Adam is not filled but with dust. And Allah returns to him who repents"
"606","A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"
"607","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Whoever spends two things in Allah's Cause"
"608","I proceeded till I entered upon `Umar (and while I was sitting there), his gate-keeper Yarfa came to him and said,  `Uthman"
"609","Anas reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If the son of Adam were to possess two valleys of riches. he would long for the third one. And the stomach of the son of Adam is not filled but with dust. And Allah returns to him who repents"
"610","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Allah created Adam in His picture"
"611","Jabir b. 'Abdullah reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying while the bier of Sa'd b. Mu'adh was placed before them:The Throne of the most Gracious shook at the death of Sa'd b. Mu'adh"
"612","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said. While I was sleeping"
"613","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, The boy is for the owner of the bed."""""
"614","Hakim bin Hizam said, I asked Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) for something"
"615","I heard Allah's Messengd-r..b..!rdL saying, lf Allah wants tof dof good tof a person"
"616","A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"
"617","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""A man keeps on asking others for something till he comes on the Day of Resurrection without any piece of flesh on his face."" The Prophet (ﷺ) added, ""On the Day of Resurrection, the Sun will come near (to, the people) to such an extent that the sweat will reach up to the middle of the ears, so, when all the people are in that state, they will ask Adam for help, and then Moses, and then Muhammad (p.b.u.h) ."" The sub-narrator added ""Muhammad will intercede with Allah to judge amongst the people. He will proceed on till he will hold the ring of the door (of Paradise) and then Allah will exalt him to Maqam Mahmud (the privilege of intercession, etc.). And all the people of the gathering will send their praises to Allah."
"618","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, ""If Allah makes us victorious, our encamping place will be Al-Khaif, the place where the infidels took an oath to be loyal to Heathenism (by boycotting Banu Hashim, the Prophet's folk)."
"619","This hadith has been narrated on the authority of A'mash through a different chain of transmitters"
"620","I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, Nothing is left of the prophetism except Al-Mubashshirat."" They asked"
"621","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, The son of Adam (i.e. man) grows old and so also two (desires) grow old with him"
"622","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, ""If Adam's son had a valley full of gold, he would like to have two valleys, for nothing fills his mouth except dust. And Allah forgives him who repents to Him."""
"623","I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, While I was sleeping"
"624","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Allah created Adam in His picture"
"625","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, The thing I am afraid of most for your sake"
"626","Ahnaf b. Qais reported:While I was in the company of the (elites) of Quraiah, Abu Dharr came there and he was saying: Give glad tidings to the hoarders of riches that their backs would be branded (so deeply) that (the hot Iron) would come out of their sides, and when the backs of their necks would be branded, it would come out of their foreheads. He (Abu Dharr) then went away and sat down. I asked who he was. They said: He is Abu Dharr. I went to him and said to him: What is this that I heard from you which you were saying before? He said: I said nothing but only that which I heard from their Prophet (ﷺ). I again said: What do you say about this gift? He said: Take it, for today it is a help. But when it becomes a price for your religion, then abandon it"
"627","Some Ansdri persons asked fof (something) from Allah's Messenge *-r.+r, -ur- alld he gave them. The again askeC him f(something) and h again gave them. And then they aske him and he gave them again till all that was with him finished. And then h said, If I had anything"
"628","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, O Allah! Give food to the family of Muhammad."""""
"629","rr i While I was walking with the Prophett pte;-.lrut- whof was wearing aNajrdni Burd (outgarment) with a thick hern"
"630","Anas b. Malik is reported as saying:Abu Talha was the one among the Ansar of Medina who possessed the largest property and among his property he valued most was his garden known as Bairaha' which was opposite the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) often visited it and he drank of its sweet water. When this verse was revealed: You will never attain righteousness till you give freely of what you love"" (iii. 91)"
"631","This hadith has been narrated on the authority of Hisham with the same chain of transmitters. And in the hadith transmitted by Abu Usama the words are: She did not make any will"
"632","r:-. replied, I give tof such people as are still close tZ.rneBooll. ot Za*at tof the period of ignorance ( i.e. the have recently embraced Islam and Fait is still weak in thei hearts). Won't yo be pleased tof see the people gof with forhrne"
"633","The Prophet (ﷺ) sent for the Ansar (and when they came), he asked, 'Is there any stranger amongst you? They said"
"634","On the day of the Conquest of Mecca, when the Prophet (ﷺ) had given (from the booty) the Quraish, the Ansar said, By Allah"
"635","When it was the day (of the battle) of Hunain, the tributes of Hawazin and Ghatafan and others, along with their animals and offspring (and wives) came to fight against the Prophet (ﷺ) The Prophet (ﷺ) had with him, ten thousand men and some of the Tulaqa. The companions fled, leaving the Prophet (ﷺ) alone. The Prophet then made two calls which were clearly distinguished from each other. He turned right and said, O the group of Ansar!"" They said"
"636","When Allah gave to His Apostle the war booty on the day of Hunain, he distributed that booty amongst those whose hearts have been (recently) reconciled (to Islam), but did not give anything to the Ansar. So they seemed to have felt angry and sad as they did not get the same as other people had got. The Prophet (ﷺ) then delivered a sermon before them, saying, O"
"637","On the day (of the battle) of Hunain, Allah's Messengps* at s)- favoured some people in the distribution of the booty (tof the exclusion of others); he gave Al-Aqra' bin Hdbis one hundred camels and he gave 'Uyaina the same amount, and alsof gave tof some of the eminent Arabs, giving them preference in this regard. Then a person came and said, By Allah"
"638","While Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) was distributing the booty at Al-Ja'rana, somebody said to him ""Be just (in your distribution)."" The Prophet (ﷺ) replied, ""Verily I would be miserable if I did not act justly."""
"639","Alie sent a piece of gold tof the Prophett F:*..r,..r- whof distributed it among fou person: Al-Aqra' bin Hdbis Al-Hanzalie from the tribe of Al- Mujasha'i, 'Uyaina bin Bad Al-Fazari, Zaid At-Ta'i whof belonged tof (the tribe of) Bani Nabhdn, and 'Alqama bin 'Ul6that Al-'Amiri whof belonged tof (the tribe of) Bani Kil6b. Sof the Quraish and the Ansd became angry and said, He (i.e. the Prophett & +.rr"
"640","`Ali bin Abi Talib sent a piece of gold not yet taken out of its ore, in a tanned leather container to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) . Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) distributed that amongst four Persons: 'Uyaina bin Badr, Aqra bin H`Abis, Zaid Al-Khail and the fourth was either Alqama or Amir bin at-Tufail. On that, one of his companions said, We are more deserving of this (gold) than these (persons)."" When that news reached the Prophet (ﷺ) "
"641","I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, While I was sleeping"
"642","While we were with Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) a bedouin got up and said, O Allah's Messenger (ﷺ)! Settle my case according to Allah's Book (Laws)."" Then his opponent got up and said"
"643","I relate the traditions of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) to you for I would rather fall from the sky than attribute something to him falsely. But when I tell you a thing which is between you and me, then no doubt, war is guile. I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, In the last days of this world there will appear some young foolish people who will use (in their claim) the best speech of all people (i.e. the Qur'an) and they will abandon Islam as an arrow going through the game. Their belief will not go beyond their throats (i.e. they will have practically no belief)"
"644","I asked Sahl bin Hunaif, Did you hear the Prophet (ﷺ) saying anything about Al-Khawarij?"" He said"
"645","Abdullah b. Mas'ud reported that Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said:There is none amongst you with whom is not an attache from amongst the jinn (devil). They (the Companions) said: Allah's Messenger, with you too? Thereupon he said: Yes, but Allah helps me against him and so I am safe from his hand and he does not command me but for good"
"646","Anas reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If the son of Adam were to possess two valleys of riches. he would long for the third one. And the stomach of the son of Adam is not filled but with dust. And Allah returns to him who repents"
"647","The Prophet (ﷺ) passed by a fallen date and said, ""Were it not for my doubt that this might have been given in charity, I would have eaten it."" And narrated Abu Huraira the Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""I found a datefruit fallen on my bed."""
"648","Some meat was presented tof the Prophett or,r- d-r.+r and it had been given tof Barira (the freed slave-girl of 'Aisha rd"
"649","Once the Prophet (ﷺ) went to `Aisha and asked her whether she had something (to eat). She said that she had nothing except the mutton which Um 'Atiyya had sent to (Barirah) in charity. The Prophet (ﷺ) said that it had reached its destination (i.e. it is no longer an object of charity.)"
"650","Abdullah b. Mas'ud reported that Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said:There is none amongst you with whom is not an attache from amongst the jinn (devil). They (the Companions) said: Allah's Messenger, with you too? Thereupon he said: Yes, but Allah helps me against him and so I am safe from his hand and he does not command me but for good"
"651","Asma' reported Allah's Messenger (way peace be upon him) as saying (to her):Spend and do not calculate, (for) Allah would calculate in your case; and do not hoard, otherwise Allah would be withholding from you"
